invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_field.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the field's inverse multiplies p256_wide_inverse's answer by a word
  off 2^768 mod p, so every inverse leaves the Montgomery domain wrong.
  bin/p256_equiv_test holds the field's inverse to p256_field.c's, and
  tools/p256_wide.py, which make lint-p256-wide runs, recomputes the
  constant.

--- old
    {UINT64_C(0xfffffffd0000000a), UINT64_C(0xffffffedfffffff7), UINT64_C(0x00000005fffffffc),
--- new
    {UINT64_C(0xfffffffd0000000b), UINT64_C(0xffffffedfffffff7), UINT64_C(0x00000005fffffffc),
